WEBVTT

00:00:03.264 --> 00:00:04.875
[singsongy]:
Boring.

00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:07.399
KING PEPPY: Until one day,
someone made a sound.

00:00:07.442 --> 00:00:08.966
-[plays note]
-[Trolls oohing]

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.882
Our ancestors were
so inspired by the sound,

00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:14.406
-they took six strings.
-[melody plays]

00:00:14.449 --> 00:00:19.150
And those six strings had
the power to control all music.

00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:20.542
They could play anything.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:22.196
[harp strumming]

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.329
-[different styles playing]
-Techno, funk, classical,

00:00:24.372 --> 00:00:26.897
country, hard rock and pop.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.682
And every kind of music
in between.

00:00:29.725 --> 00:00:31.423
There was something
for everyone.

00:00:31.466 --> 00:00:33.120
It was one big party.

00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:34.469
TROLLS:
Yay!

00:00:34.513 --> 00:00:36.036
KING PEPPY:
But little by little,

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.560
Trolls became intolerant
of each other's music.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:39.866
-[Trolls arguing]
-TROLL: I want it!

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.086
-I want to listen to techno!
-No fair!

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:43.870
Hey, y'all, I want country.

00:00:43.914 --> 00:00:46.264
KING PEPPY: They fought
over what kind of music

00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:47.874
the strings would play.

00:00:47.918 --> 00:00:50.529
The elders realized
there was but one solution.

00:00:50.572 --> 00:00:52.748
TROLLS: Blah,
blah-blah-blah-blah. Agreed.

00:00:52.792 --> 00:00:55.273
KING PEPPY:
Each tribe would take a string

00:00:55.316 --> 00:00:57.753
-and go their separate ways.
-[Trolls chattering]

00:00:59.364 --> 00:01:03.498
Those six tribes have lived
in isolation ever since.

00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:06.284
Techno, Country, Rock,

00:01:06.327 --> 00:01:08.286
Classical, Funk,

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:11.115
and us, the Pop Trolls.

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:14.596
Now Barb's announcement
makes sense.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.076
She wants to reunite
the strings

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.818
so the Troll World
can be one big party again.

00:01:18.862 --> 00:01:20.341
Wait, that's all you heard?

00:01:20.385 --> 00:01:22.126
-One big party?
-[chuckles]: Yeah!

00:01:22.169 --> 00:01:24.084
It's when all the Trolls
lived in harmony.

00:01:24.128 --> 00:01:26.565
And what's more important
than living in harmony?

00:01:26.608 --> 00:01:27.871
Well, I heard fighting.

00:01:27.914 --> 00:01:29.350
The strings together
leads to fighting.

00:01:29.394 --> 00:01:30.656
KING PEPPY:
Exactly, Branch.

00:01:30.699 --> 00:01:33.354
That's why we need
to keep our string safe.

00:01:33.398 --> 00:01:35.617
♪

00:01:39.273 --> 00:01:40.274
Behold!

00:01:40.318 --> 00:01:43.016
The pop music string.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:46.019
FEMALE STRING VOICE:
♪ Oh, yeah.

00:01:46.063 --> 00:01:48.500
-[Trolls gasping]
-[magic jingling]

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.939
It's beautiful.

00:01:52.983 --> 00:01:54.506
KING PEPPY:
And powerful.

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:57.901
Which is why we can't let it
fall into the wrong hands.

00:01:57.944 --> 00:02:00.251
And we won't.
Not on my watch.

00:02:00.294 --> 00:02:02.644
What we need is a plan.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:03.907
Don't worry.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.997
I've been preparing
for this day for years.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:08.476
-We run.
-Run?

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.477
And hide.

00:02:09.521 --> 00:02:11.088
On it.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:14.178
But we don't even know what
we're running and hiding from.

00:02:14.221 --> 00:02:17.833
We're hiding from Barb and
all the other different Trolls.

00:02:17.877 --> 00:02:19.661
POPPY:
You're assuming the worst about

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.228
someone you haven't even met.

00:02:21.272 --> 00:02:24.579
-You're not listening to me.
-You're not listening to me.

00:02:24.623 --> 00:02:27.365
-I'm your father!
-And I'm the queen.

00:02:27.408 --> 00:02:28.975
Uh, father trumps queen.

00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:31.673
Now, there's no time
to debate this. Let's go.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.414
Come along, Branch.

00:02:33.458 --> 00:02:35.199
Well, I, um...

00:02:36.243 --> 00:02:38.419
We're all Trolls.

00:02:38.463 --> 00:02:40.682
Differences don't matter.

00:02:41.596 --> 00:02:42.858
[growling]

00:02:42.902 --> 00:02:44.860
Oh, look how cute you are!

00:02:44.904 --> 00:02:46.993
Barb is gonna love
your new look.

00:02:47.037 --> 00:02:48.908
Tell her I look forward
to helping her

00:02:48.952 --> 00:02:50.518
plan the world's biggest party.

00:02:50.562 --> 00:02:51.606
-Poppy.
-[screams]

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:53.565
-What are you doing?
-Oh. Nothing.

00:02:53.608 --> 00:02:55.001
SHEILA B:
Ooh!

00:02:55.045 --> 00:02:57.438
Poppy's busted.

00:02:57.482 --> 00:02:58.483
[shushing]

00:02:58.526 --> 00:03:00.267
BRANCH:
Sneaking out to meet Barb?

00:03:00.311 --> 00:03:01.529
Headed into enemy territory?

00:03:01.573 --> 00:03:02.530
She's not the enemy.

00:03:02.574 --> 00:03:04.315
She's a queen, the same as me.

00:03:04.358 --> 00:03:06.317
-[growling]
-[grunting]

00:03:07.231 --> 00:03:08.623
Bye-bye, little bat.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:11.191
Your dad just told us
that Queen Barb is bad news.

00:03:11.235 --> 00:03:12.671
Well, my dad
doesn't know everything.

00:03:12.714 --> 00:03:14.281
He knows more about this.

00:03:14.325 --> 00:03:16.544
You didn't even know there was
a string until this morning.

00:03:16.588 --> 00:03:19.199
He may be fine in a world where
everybody lives in isolation,

00:03:19.243 --> 00:03:21.114
-but I'm not.
-Well, but we don't know

00:03:21.158 --> 00:03:23.421
anything about
the other Trolls.

00:03:23.464 --> 00:03:24.988
Well, we know they're Trolls.

00:03:25.031 --> 00:03:26.772
Branch, look around
Troll Village.

00:03:26.815 --> 00:03:29.209
Everybody's different, even us.

00:03:29.253 --> 00:03:31.211
[distant sneeze]

00:03:31.255 --> 00:03:32.212
Oh.

00:03:32.256 --> 00:03:33.648
Did you hear something?

00:03:33.692 --> 00:03:35.346
Stop trying
to change the subject.

00:03:35.389 --> 00:03:37.565
Look, being queen means
having a lot of power,

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:39.959
and it's my job
to use it for good.

00:03:40.003 --> 00:03:41.569
I can't stay home
when I know there's

00:03:41.613 --> 00:03:45.182
a world full of different
Trolls out there just like us.

00:03:46.052 --> 00:03:48.185
[sighs] This is a terrible idea

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.926
that will most likely
blow up in your face.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.928
-Okay, bye.
-What?

00:03:59.413 --> 00:04:00.980
[groans]

00:04:05.115 --> 00:04:06.116
[grunts]

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:08.814
And I guess
I'm coming with you.

00:04:08.857 --> 00:04:10.816
[sobs]:
Oh! Thank you.

00:04:10.859 --> 00:04:13.036
I really didn't want
to go by myself.

00:04:13.079 --> 00:04:15.255
-Road trip!
-Yeah!

00:04:20.565 --> 00:04:22.784
♪

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.407
They areall different.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:40.324
[gasps softly] A-And this one
looks a little bit like me.

00:04:42.152 --> 00:04:43.370
[gasps]

00:04:43.414 --> 00:04:45.068
We even have the same hat!

00:04:45.111 --> 00:04:47.679
[echoing]: ...same hat,
same hat, same hat!

00:04:47.722 --> 00:04:49.333
♪

